<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Cyrene under Magas</h1><p class="st-meta">276 BCE – 250 BCE (approx.) · capital Cyrene</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The breakaway Hellenistic kingdom of Magas, stepson of Ptolemy I, who ruled Cyrenaica independently of Egypt.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magas-of-cyrene">Magas</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I's</a> queen <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/euesperides">Berenice</a> I by an earlier marriage, became governor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> around 300 BCE after a revolt there was suppressed. On the death of his stepfather he grew restive and around 276 BCE proclaimed himself king, breaking away from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magas-of-cyrene">Magas</a> married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apama-wife-of-magas">Apama</a>, daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid</a> king Antiochus I, and in alliance with the Seleucids marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the mid-270s BCE, but was forced back by a Libyan revolt. He ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pentapolis-cyrenaica">Pentapolis</a> for decades, minting his own coins. Later he made peace with his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-ii-philadelphus">Ptolemy II</a> and betrothed his daughter <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/euesperides">Berenice</a> to the heir, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iii-euergetes">Ptolemy III</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magas-of-cyrene">Magas</a> died around 250 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apama-wife-of-magas">Apama</a> invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-the-fair">Demetrius the Fair</a> to marry <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/euesperides">Berenice</a> and rule, but Berenice had him killed. She then married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iii-euergetes">Ptolemy III</a> in 246 BCE, reuniting <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and became the queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berenice-ii">Berenice II</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-cyrene-under-magas.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Cyrene under Magas" width="320" height="152"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magas_as_king_of_Kyrene,_circa_282_or_275_to_261_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>276 BCE – 250 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cyrene</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Magas, Demetrius the Fair, Berenice II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Magas of Cyrene</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-263&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cyrene-under-magas" aria-label="Kingdom of Cyrene under Magas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5240 985 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Cyrene under Magas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5560 1241L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5560 1241h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5560 1241h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cyrene. <a href="/atlas?year=-263&amp;focus=kingdom-of-cyrene-under-magas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
